  title={Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) Model for Predicting Patient-Specific Drug Response in Precision Oncology}, 
  year={2026},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-6},
  abstract={The study includes a model based on Graph Convolutional Network (GCN) to predict patient-specific drug responses in precision oncology. The proposed model will combine multi-omics information, interactions among genes, and relationships between drugs and their targets into one single graph to learn complicated biological interactions that affect treatment outcomes. The GCN is able to capture both molecular-level and patient-level variations by utilizing big data pharmacogenomic data, including GDSC, CCLE, and TCGA. The results of the experiment show that the presented approach is better than the standard machine learning and deep learning models in terms of predictive accuracy and interpretability. The model does not only correlate well with experimental drug response values but also determines key genes and pathways that are linked with response to the therapeutic sensitivity. This paper has identified the possibilities of GCNs in creating customized cancer therapy plans and improving precision medicine by using biologically motivated computational modeling.},
