  abstract={A growing number of assistive technologies have been developed to assist visually impaired individuals in their daily lives. We developed a smart blind stick that uses Raspberry Pi technology to enable blind users to navigate their environment more independently and safely. In the proposed system, ultrasonic sensors detect obstacles, a GPS module tracks locations in real-time, and a buzzer warns users when an obstacle is detected. As the central processor, the Raspberry Pi synchronises sensor inputs and manages data transmission via IoT infrastructure efficiently. In addition, users' location can be tracked in real-time by caregivers or family members via cloud connectivity. By using this holistic approach, users and their guardians are able to address both physical navigation challenges and feel more secure and reassured. A prototype of the product was tested in a variety of real-world scenarios, demonstrating accurate obstacle detection, timely alerts, and reliable GPS tracking. Researchers found that the device is potentially cost-effective, scalable, and practical for improving the lives of visually impaired people and increasing their independence.},
