  booktitle={2025 2nd International Conference on Emerging Trends in Electronic Devices and Computational Techniques (EDCT)}, 
  title={Carcinogenic Gene Prediction Using Fuzzy Random Forest Classifier Powered by Z Score (Frf ${}^{\mathrm{Z}\_\text{Sc }}$)}, 
  year={2025},
  volume={},
  number={},
  pages={1-7},
  abstract={In recent days, medical science is considering the disease cancer as the most challenging one having significant mortality rate. It is observed that some gene expression levels vary significantly when normal cells turn into cancer cells. The identification of cancer-mediating genes is crucial for understanding cancer progression, diagnosis, and the development of targeted therapies. Traditional statistical methods and machine learning models often struggle with the inherent uncertainty and noise in biological data. The Random Forest (RF) technique is nowadays being used in the field of bioinformatics which ensembles decision trees and incorporates feature selection. This paper presents a novel approach which combines statistical method Z-test followed by Fuzzy Random Forest (FRF) algorithm to identify cancer-mediating genes. By integrating fuzzy logic with the Random Forest model, FRF effectively handles the uncertainty in gene expression data, leading to more robust and interpretable results. We apply this method to a dataset of gene expression profiles from cancerous and normal tissues, demonstrating its superiority over traditional methods in identifying key cancerrelated genes. The accuracy of the model has been established with the F1 score, accuracy score.},
  keywords={Radio broadcasting;Frequency modulation;System-on-chip;Radio frequency;Protocols;HTTP;Modulation;Radio broadcasting;Radio communication;Frequency modulation;Fuzzy Random Forest;Cancer-Mediating Genes;Gene Expression;Machine Learning;Bioinformatics;Fuzzy Logic},
  doi={10.1109/EDCT65302.2025.11496159},
