  abstract={ML as a part of AI builds up numerous statistical probabilistic and optimization techniques that qualify computers to learn from past experience and to detect patterns that are hard-to-observe in large noisy or complicated data sets thus it is well positioned for applications in medicine with a focus on the proteomic and genomic complexity as such it sees use increasingly in cancer diagnosis and detection cancer is often described as a heterogeneous disease containing many different subtypes the early diagnosis and prognosis of a cancer type has become a necessity in cancer research as it promises to facilitate subsequent clinical management of patients hence classifying cancer patients into high or low risk groups is one of the necessary foundations in which many teams of researchers especially in biomedical and bioinformatics fields apply into study the application of machine learning ml methods hence these techniques have been exploited for the intention of modeling the development and therapy of cancerous conditions furthermore ml tools can actually identify critical features from complicated datasets various such techniques including ANNs, BNs, SVMs and DTs have been extensively applied in cancer research for predictive model developments aiming at effective and accurate decision making three indicators including prediction accuracy values the f-measure metric and auc values are utilized to compare the performance of these five classification models and hence the model of this study is approved to possess clinical values in practical applications. The model we created to identify the type has an accuracy of 97%.},
