  abstract={The success application of deep studying frameworks to the complicated scientific imaging area has been widely a hit. The deep learning framework for Predicting cancer outcome (PCO) using critical imaging statistics is one such software. This paper proposes a revolutionary approach to augment PCO performance. The model is based totally on a unique -branch structure, including an automatic feature extraction department and a context or venture-particular department. The strength of function Extraction documents the overall performance of the 2-branch version in predicting the affected person’s cancer effects. Similarly, the version functions facts augmentation to address the imbalanced pattern length and consists of the use of class algorithms to lessen the fake superb and false bad costs. The proposed version is evaluated on an extensive dataset collected from a synthetic cohort taken a look at with clinical imaging records. Results show that the version carried out an excellent 97.4% accuracy charge with low mean squared error values of zero.087, indicating the capacity of the proposed framework to noticeably improve the accuracy of cancer outcome prediction fashions.},
